        "id": 1000107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-09-06T15:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "* Logging is probably a good idea when we detect some of these error conditions.  I will file a bug for it and other cleanups.\n\n* I think (0, 0) is the error that we really can\u0027t get out of.  We could add a delay but I\u0027m not sure how long to wait.  What I decided is that it\u0027s OK that this function do nothing in that case.  Then we\u0027ll fail to write to the i2c port later in the PMIC code and issue a full PMIC reset which should unwedge everything (except if the battery is dragging down the clock--but we haven\u0027t seen that).\n\n* If we\u0027re going to add logging checking that we actually drove the lines low seems reasonable.\n\n* Good suggestion on testing.  Would make it much more reproducible / easier to capture logs.\n\n\nFrom traces I captured it did look as if sending the STOP bit did properly reset things even if it was in a weird place in the transaction.  With bitbang testing we could really confirm that, though.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAPn//0OQ\u003d",
      "revId": "e54ac8da053cd525946d9c7410405fe1686c5400",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
