      "message": "If the device is midway through sending _us_ data and that data is all zeros then yes.\n\nTechnically we could send a stop bit as soon as we see sda go high and then abort this loop.  That should work for all devices that we know about.  Hard to know which is better, but throwing the extra clocks on there seemed like it should hurt in any cases that I could think about.",
